-- === 1. Beijing Daxing Airport ===
UPDATE posts SET content = '
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:12px;background:#f8f6f3;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:32px;">
  <div><strong style="color:#c09020;font-size:0.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;">Timeline</strong><br/>2024–2025</div>
  <div><strong style="color:#c09020;font-size:0.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;">Products</strong><br/>Curved Baffle System</div>
  <div><strong style="color:#c09020;font-size:0.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;">Scope</strong><br/>2,400 sqm Retail Cladding</div>
  <div><strong style="color:#c09020;font-size:0.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;">Services</strong><br/>Design, Manufacturing, Installation Guidance</div>
</div>

<h2>Project Overview</h2>
<p>Beijing Daxing International Airport — one of the world''s largest single-terminal airport buildings — required a ceiling and wall cladding solution for its premium retail store zones. The design brief demanded flowing, organic ceiling geometry that would create a distinctive shopping environment while meeting stringent aviation-sector fire safety and acoustic standards.</p>

<h2>The Challenge</h2>
<p>Retail spaces within airport terminals face unique constraints: extremely high foot traffic (thousands of passengers daily), strict fire safety requirements (Class A1 non-combustible), and the need for rapid installation during limited construction windows. Additionally, the curved architectural language of Zaha Hadid''s terminal design required every ceiling panel to follow a unique radius — no two panels were identical.</p>

<img src="https://prancebuilding.com/lifisher-m4842/1782288890933-beijing-airport-retail-store-curved-baffle-cladding-project-3.jpg" alt="Beijing Daxing Airport curved baffle ceiling overview" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0;" />

<h2>Our Solution</h2>
<p>We engineered a custom curved aluminum baffle system using CNC precision bending technology. Each baffle was individually numbered and mapped to its exact installation position, ensuring seamless assembly on-site. The system was fabricated from 1.0mm aluminum alloy 3003-H24 and finished with a three-coat PVDF coating system for long-term color stability under intense terminal lighting.</p>

<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin:16px 0;">
  <img src="https://prancebuilding.com/lifisher-m4842/1782288887485-beijing-airport-retail-store-curved-baffle-cladding-project-2.jpg" alt="Curved baffle system detail" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;" />
  <img src="https://prancebuilding.com/lifisher-m4842/1782288884558-beijing-airport-retail-store-curved-baffle-cladding-project-1.jpg" alt="Retail storefront ceiling installation" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;" />
</div>

<h2>Lighting Integration</h2>
<p>The baffle system was designed with integrated LED lighting channels, allowing recessed spotlights and linear ambient lighting to be embedded directly into the ceiling profile. This eliminated the need for separate lighting fixtures, creating a clean, uninterrupted ceiling plane that enhanced the premium retail atmosphere.</p>

<img src="https://prancebuilding.com/lifisher-m4842/1782288893521-beijing-airport-retail-store-curved-baffle-cladding-project-4.jpg" alt="Lighting integration in curved baffle ceiling" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0;" />

<h2>Technical Specifications</h2>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:16px 0;">
  <tr style="background:#f8f6f3;"><td style="padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Material</td><td style="padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">1.0mm Aluminum Alloy 3003-H24</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Surface Finish</td><td style="padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Three-coat PVDF, RAL custom color</td></tr>
  <tr style="background:#f8f6f3;"><td style="padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Coverage Area</td><td style="padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">2,400 sqm</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Fire Rating</td><td style="padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Class A1 (non-combustible)</td></tr>
  <tr style="background:#f8f6f3;"><td style="padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Baffle Profile</td><td style="padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Custom CNC curved, variable radii</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Installation</td><td style="padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Modular clip-in system, numbered panels</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Results</h2>
<p>The curved baffle system was installed across all retail zones within the project timeline, delivering a premium aesthetic that complements the airport''s iconic architecture. The modular installation approach reduced on-site labor by approximately 30% compared to traditional custom ceiling solutions, and the PVDF finish ensures the ceiling will maintain its appearance for decades with minimal maintenance.</p>
