-- === 3. Singapore Changi Airport ===
UPDATE posts SET content = '
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:12px;background:#f8f6f3;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:32px;">
  <div><strong style="color:#c09020;font-size:0.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;">Timeline</strong><br/>2024</div>
  <div><strong style="color:#c09020;font-size:0.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;">Products</strong><br/>Perforated Aluminum Panels</div>
  <div><strong style="color:#c09020;font-size:0.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;">Scope</strong><br/>Terminal Ceiling & Acoustics</div>
  <div><strong style="color:#c09020;font-size:0.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;">Services</strong><br/>Acoustic Design, Custom Perforation</div>
</div>

<h2>Project Overview</h2>
<p>Singapore Changi Airport — consistently ranked among the world''s best airports — required custom perforated aluminum panels that serve dual functional and aesthetic purposes. The panels needed to manage airflow patterns within the terminal while simultaneously creating a distinctive visual identity through variable perforation patterns.</p>

<h2>The Challenge</h2>
<p>Airport terminals generate significant ambient noise from HVAC systems, passenger movement, and announcements. Changi''s design team specified a ceiling solution that would reduce reverberation time by at least 12dB while maintaining an open, visually dynamic ceiling plane. The perforation pattern also needed to transition smoothly from dense (high acoustic absorption) to sparse (decorative) across different terminal zones.</p>

<img src="https://prancebuilding.com/lifisher-m4842/1760579215486-singapore-changi-airport-perforated-aluminum-panel-project-11.jpg" alt="Singapore Changi Airport terminal ceiling with perforated panels" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0;" />

<h2>Our Solution</h2>
<p>We developed CNC-perforated aluminum panels with variable hole patterns ranging from 2mm to 8mm diameter. Each panel was individually programmed to achieve the precise open-area ratio required for its specific zone — denser perforation near gates and waiting areas for maximum acoustic absorption, graduating to wider patterns in circulation corridors for visual continuity.</p>

<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin:16px 0;">
  <img src="https://prancebuilding.com/lifisher-m4842/1760579205502-singapore-changi-airport-perforated-aluminum-panel-project-3.jpg" alt="Custom perforation pattern detail" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;" />
  <img src="https://prancebuilding.com/lifisher-m4842/1760579207407-singapore-changi-airport-perforated-aluminum-panel-project-5.jpg" alt="Perforated panel close-up" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;" />
</div>

<h2>Acoustic Performance</h2>
<p>Backed with mineral wool acoustic insulation, the perforated panel system achieved a Noise Reduction Coefficient (NRC) of 0.85 — exceeding the 12dB reduction target. The panels also serve as airflow management surfaces, allowing conditioned air to pass through while maintaining a clean visual ceiling plane.</p>

<img src="https://prancebuilding.com/lifisher-m4842/1762305671643-singapore-changi-airport-perforated-aluminum-panel-project-8.jpg" alt="Acoustic and fire safety performance" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0;" />

<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin:16px 0;">
  <img src="https://prancebuilding.com/lifisher-m4842/1760579193245-singapore-changi-airport-perforated-aluminum-panel-project-1.jpg" alt="Completed terminal wide view" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;" />
  <img src="https://prancebuilding.com/lifisher-m4842/1760579204537-singapore-changi-airport-perforated-aluminum-panel-project-2.jpg" alt="Final ceiling effect" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;" />
</div>

<h2>Technical Specifications</h2>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:16px 0;">
  <tr style="background:#f8f6f3;"><td style="padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Material</td><td style="padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">1.5mm Aluminum Alloy 5005-H34</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Perforation</td><td style="padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Variable 2mm–8mm CNC holes, zone-programmed</td></tr>
  <tr style="background:#f8f6f3;"><td style="padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">NRC Rating</td><td style="padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">0.85 (with mineral wool backing)</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Surface Finish</td><td style="padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Powder coating, RAL 9003 Signal White</td></tr>
  <tr style="background:#f8f6f3;"><td style="padding:10px 14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Fire Rating</td><td style="padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #e8e4df;">Class A1 non-combustible</td></tr>
</table>
