<h2>Project Overview</h2>
<p>Emaar Properties'' Beachfront development in Dubai comprises the Bayview and Seapoint residential towers — a landmark waterfront complex requiring a comprehensive ceiling solution across lobbies, corridors, parking areas, and amenity spaces. With 50,000 sqm of ceiling area, this represents one of the largest single-project metal ceiling installations in the Middle East.</p>

<h2>The Challenge</h2>
<p>Dubai''s extreme climate — summer temperatures exceeding 50°C, high humidity, and saline coastal air — demands ceiling materials that resist corrosion, thermal expansion, and UV degradation over decades. Additionally, the project required a unified design language across vastly different space types: from luxury residential lobbies with premium finishes to utilitarian parking structures requiring heavy-duty performance.</p>

<img src="https://prancebuilding.com/lifisher-m0/1776327516736-dubaiemaarbeachfrontbayviewandseapointmetalceilingproject3.jpg" alt="Dubai Emaar Beachfront building exterior" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0;" />

<h2>Our Solution</h2>
<p>We engineered a multi-product ceiling package tailored to each zone''s specific requirements: premium lay-in tiles with acoustic perforation for lobby areas, moisture-resistant clip-in panels for wet zones and pools, and heavy-duty baffle ceilings for parking structures. All systems share a unified color palette and are manufactured with marine-grade pre-treatment to withstand Dubai''s coastal environment.</p>

<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin:16px 0;">
